                <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-3">Ipamorelin is a synthetic research peptide supplied for laboratory and in-vitro research applications. It belongs to a class of compounds known as growth hormone secretagogues and has been investigated extensively for its ability to stimulate the release of growth hormone through the growth hormone secretagogue receptor.</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-3">Originally developed during research into selective growth hormone-releasing compounds, Ipamorelin has been studied in cellular, animal and human pharmacological models. Research has examined Ipamorelin in relation to growth hormone secretion, receptor activity, pharmacokinetics and broader endocrine signalling.</p>
